          <p class="eyebrow">First, the basics</p>
          <h2>What is mineral sunscreen?</h2>
          <p>Mineral sunscreens use zinc oxide, titanium dioxide, or both as active sunscreen ingredients. These ingredients help protect skin from ultraviolet radiation. Broad-spectrum products are designed to protect against both UVA and UVB rays.</p>
          <p>Mineral sunscreen can be a useful choice for people who prefer these active ingredients, but the texture and finish vary by formula. Some products blend in more easily than others.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="panel">
          <h3>Why does a white cast happen?</h3>
          <p>Zinc oxide and titanium dioxide are mineral particles that can leave a pale appearance on skin. The effect depends on the formula, the amount applied, the particle characteristics, and your skin tone.</p>
          <p>A tinted formula can help reduce the visible contrast. No product can guarantee an invisible finish on every skin tone, so testing the formula in natural light is useful.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

